**Day 42: HTTP Protocol & REST Concepts**  

**Topic:**  
Understanding HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE), status codes, and REST principles. Practical observation of HTTP requests/responses using Postman and browser DevTools.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Learn core HTTP methods and their purposes.  
• Understand RESTful architecture and its constraints.  
• Interpret HTTP status codes for troubleshooting.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Use Postman to send HTTP requests to public APIs.  
• Analyze responses using browser DevTools.  
• Document observed status codes and request/response structures.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• Statelessness in REST.  
• Idempotency of HTTP methods (e.g., PUT vs. POST).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• Not applicable (focus on HTTP/REST).  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Fetching data from a weather API (GET).  
• Submitting a form to a server (POST).  
• Updating user profile details (PUT).  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• Postman  
• Browser DevTools (Network tab)  

**Summary:**  
Explored HTTP methods, REST principles, and status codes through hands-on API testing. Gained proficiency in debugging requests/responses using Postman and DevTools.  

